    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdulli</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an Alpine people in</i> Sabaudia, Inscr. ap. <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 20,
				24, § 137</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8, 3,
				20</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdullīnus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				Medulli, Medullian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Medullini te feret aura noti,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Alpine wind</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 5, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
